IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ta-nouns`
IMPORT `ta-logic`

-- Terrorism Act 2000, Part III, sections 21CA to 21CF -- layer 1: one business in the regulated sector may pass information to
-- another, if the police have been told; what the notification does for the duty to disclose; the limits of that relief.
-- "A business in the regulated sector" and "relevant undertaking" turn on Schedule 3A, which is not among the sources: facts
-- the caller states.  Each subsection answers on its own (E1 option C).
-- Reading F8: "where applicable" in s 21CA(1)(b) is read with s 21CA(7): condition 5 applies unless a constable made the request.
-- Reading F9: a report sent on the last day of the applicable period is sent "before the end" of it.
-- Reading F10: a constable's variation of the 28 days takes effect only by written notice to the person who made the required notification.

§ `Part III Terrorist Property -- Voluntary disclosures within the regulated sector`

§§ `s 21CA Voluntary disclosures within the regulated sector`

-- src:206 | (2) Condition 1 is that—
-- src:207 | (a) A is carrying on a business in the regulated sector as a relevant undertaking,
-- src:208 | (b) the information on which the disclosure is based came to A in the course of carrying on that business, and
-- src:209 | (c) the person to whom the information is to be disclosed (or each of them, where the disclosure is to more than one person) is also carrying on a business in the regulated sector as a relevant undertaking (whether or not of the same kind as A).
@ref s 21CA(2) (src:206-209)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Condition 1 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CA(2) condition 1 is met` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `A is carrying on a business in the regulated sector as a relevant undertaking`
           AND `the facts`'s `the information on which the disclosure is based came to A in the course of carrying on that business`
           AND `the facts`'s `each person to whom the information is to be disclosed is also carrying on a business in the regulated sector as a relevant undertaking`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition 1 is that—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:210 | (3) Condition 2 is that—
-- src:211 | (a) a constable has requested A to make the disclosure, or
-- src:212 | (b) the person to whom the information is to be disclosed (or at least one of them, where the disclosure is to more than one person) has requested A to do so.
@ref s 21CA(3) (src:210-212)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Request facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CA(3) condition 2 is met` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `a constable has requested A to make the disclosure`
           OR `the facts`'s `the person to whom the information is to be disclosed (or at least one of them) has requested A to do so`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition 2 is that—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:213 | (4) Condition 3 is that, before A makes the disclosure, the required notification has been made to a constable (see section 21CB(5) to (7)).
@ref s 21CA(4) (src:213)
GIVEN `the required notification was made to a constable before A makes the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CA(4) condition 3 is met` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the required notification was made to a constable before A makes the disclosure`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition 3 is that, before A makes the disclosure, the required notification has been made to a constable"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:214 | (5) Condition 4 is that A is satisfied that the disclosure of the information will or may assist in determining any matter in connection with—
-- src:215 | (a) a suspicion that a person is involved in the commission of a terrorist financing offence, or
-- src:216 | (b) the identification of terrorist property or of its movement or use.
@ref s 21CA(5) (src:214-216)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Assist facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CA(5) condition 4 is met` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `A is satisfied that the disclosure will or may assist in determining a matter in connection with a suspicion that a person is involved in the commission of a terrorist financing offence`
           OR `the facts`'s `A is satisfied that the disclosure will or may assist in determining a matter in connection with the identification of terrorist property or of its movement or use`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition 4 is that A is satisfied that the disclosure of the information will or may assist"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:217 | (6) Condition 5 is that, before making the disclosure request, the person making the request (or at least one of them, where the request is made by more than one person) has notified a constable that the request is to be made.
@ref s 21CA(6) (src:217)
GIVEN `before making the disclosure request, the person making the request (or at least one of them) has notified a constable that the request is to be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CA(6) condition 5 is met` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `before making the disclosure request, the person making the request (or at least one of them) has notified a constable that the request is to be made`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition 5 is that, before making the disclosure request, the person making the request"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:218 | (7) Condition 5 does not apply where the disclosure request concerned is made by a constable.
@ref s 21CA(7) (src:218)
GIVEN `the disclosure request concerned is made by a constable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CA(7) condition 5 does not apply` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disclosure request concerned is made by a constable`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition 5 does not apply where the disclosure request concerned is made by a constable." (a failed \"where\": fork F8 reads it as the only case in which condition 5 is not applicable)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:203 | (1) A person (A) may disclose information to one or more other persons if—
-- src:204 | (a) conditions 1 to 4 are met, and
-- src:205 | (b) where applicable, condition 5 is also met.
@ref s 21CA(1) (src:203-205)
GIVEN `condition 1` IS A `Condition 1 facts`
      `condition 2` IS A `Request facts`
      `condition 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `condition 4` IS A `Assist facts`
      `condition 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CA(1) A may disclose information to one or more other persons` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 21CA(2) condition 1 is met` `condition 1` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `s 21CA(3) condition 2 is met` `condition 2` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `s 21CA(4) condition 3 is met` `condition 3` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `s 21CA(5) condition 4 is met` `condition 4` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND (`s 21CA(7) condition 5 does not apply` (`condition 2`'s `a constable has requested A to make the disclosure`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
                OR `s 21CA(6) condition 5 is met` `condition 5` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person (A) may disclose information to one or more other persons if—" (a permission given "if" conditions 1 to 4 and, where applicable, 5 are met; ruling of 2026-11-05 on "if" conditions)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:219 | (8) A person may disclose information to A for the purposes of making a disclosure request if, and to the extent that, the person has reason to believe that A has in A’s possession information that will or may assist in determining any matter of the kind mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) of subsection (5).
@ref s 21CA(8) (src:219)
GIVEN `the person has reason to believe that A has in A's possession information that will or may assist in determining a matter of the kind mentioned in s 21CA(5)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CA(8) the person may disclose information to A for the purposes of making a disclosure request` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has reason to believe that A has in A's possession information that will or may assist in determining a matter of the kind mentioned in s 21CA(5)(a) or (b)`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, and to the extent that, the person has reason to believe" (the "if" is not met; the extent of the permission is not worked out here)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 21CB Disclosure requests and notifications`

-- src:221 | (1) A disclosure request must—
-- src:222 | (a) state that it is made in connection with—
-- src:223 | (i) a suspicion that a person is involved in the commission of a terrorist financing offence, or
-- src:224 | (ii) the identification of terrorist property or of its movement or use,
-- src:225 | (b) identify the person or property (so far as known),
-- src:226 | (c) describe the information that is sought from A, and
-- src:227 | (d) specify the person or persons to whom it is requested that the information is disclosed.
@ref s 21CB(1) (src:221-227)
GIVEN `the request` IS A `Request content facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CB(1) the disclosure request has the content the section requires` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the request`'s `states that it is made in connection with a suspicion of involvement in a terrorist financing offence or the identification of terrorist property or its movement or use`
           AND `the request`'s `identifies the person or property so far as known`
           AND `the request`'s `describes the information that is sought from A`
           AND `the request`'s `specifies the person or persons to whom it is requested that the information is disclosed`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A disclosure request must—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:228 | (2) Subsections (3) and (4) apply where the disclosure request is made by a person mentioned in section 21CA(3)(b).
@ref s 21CB(2) (src:228)
GIVEN `the request` IS A `Recipient request facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CB(2) subsections (3) and (4) apply to the request` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the request`'s `the request is made by a person mentioned in s 21CA(3)(b)`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (3) and (4) apply where the disclosure request is made by a person mentioned in section 21CA(3)(b)."
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:229 | (3) If the request states that it is made in connection with a suspicion that a person is involved in the commission of a terrorist financing offence, the request must also—
-- src:230 | (a) set out the grounds for the suspicion, or
-- src:231 | (b) provide such other information as the person making the request thinks appropriate for the purposes of enabling A to determine whether the information requested ought to be disclosed under section 21CA.
@ref s 21CB(3) (src:229-231)
GIVEN `the request` IS A `Recipient request facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CB(3) the request states the grounds or other information` IS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the request states that it is made in connection with a suspicion that a person is involved in the commission of a terrorist financing offence, the request must also—" (the "if" is not met: ruling of 2026-11-05)
        IF (NOT `the request`'s `the request states that it is made in connection with a suspicion of involvement in a terrorist financing offence`)
            THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the request must also— (a) set out the grounds for the suspicion, or (b) provide such other information"
        IF `the request`'s `the request sets out the grounds for the suspicion`
           OR `the request`'s `the request provides such other information as the person making it thinks appropriate for enabling A to determine whether the information ought to be disclosed`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:232 | (4) If the request states that it is made in connection with the identification of terrorist property or of its movement or use, the request must also provide such other information as the person making the request thinks appropriate for the purposes of enabling A to determine whether the information requested ought to be disclosed under section 21CA.
@ref s 21CB(4) (src:232)
GIVEN `the request` IS A `Recipient request facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CB(4) the request provides the other information` IS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the request states that it is made in connection with the identification of terrorist property or of its movement or use, the request must also provide" (the "if" is not met: ruling of 2026-11-05)
        IF (NOT `the request`'s `the request states that it is made in connection with the identification of terrorist property or of its movement or use`)
            THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the request must also provide such other information as the person making the request thinks appropriate"
        IF `the request`'s `the request provides such other information as the person making it thinks appropriate for enabling A to determine whether the information ought to be disclosed`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:233 | (5) A required notification for the purposes of section 21CA(4) must be made—
-- src:234 | (a) in the case of a disclosure request made by a constable, by the person who is to disclose information under section 21CA as a result of the request;
-- src:235 | (b) in the case of a disclosure request made by a person mentioned in section 21CA(3)(b), by the person who made the request.
@ref s 21CB(5) (src:233-235)
GIVEN `who asked` IS A `Who asked for the disclosure`
      `who made the notification` IS A `Who made the notification`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CB(5) the required notification is made by the person the subsection names` IS
    CONSIDER `who asked`
    WHEN `a constable` THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a disclosure request made by a constable, by the person who is to disclose information under section 21CA"
        IF `who made the notification` EQUALS `Person A` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a person mentioned in s 21CA(3)(b)` THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a disclosure request made by a person mentioned in section 21CA(3)(b), by the person who made the request"
        IF `who made the notification` EQUALS `Person B` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:236 | (6) In a case within subsection (5)(a), the required notification must state that information is to be disclosed under section 21CA.
@ref s 21CB(6) (src:236)
GIVEN `the notification states that information is to be disclosed under s 21CA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CB(6) the notification has the content the subsection requires` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the notification states that information is to be disclosed under s 21CA`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the required notification must state that information is to be disclosed under section 21CA"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:237 | (7) In a case within subsection (5)(b), the required notification must—
-- src:238 | (a) state that a disclosure request has been made;
-- src:239 | (b) specify the person to whom the request was made;
-- src:240 | (c) where the disclosure request to which the notification relates is made in connection with a suspicion of a person’s involvement in the commission of a terrorist financing offence, identify the person (so far as known);
-- src:241 | (d) where the disclosure request to which the notification relates is made in connection with the identification of terrorist property or of its movement or use, identify the property and the person who holds it (if known).
@ref s 21CB(7) (src:237-241)
GIVEN `the notification` IS A `Requester notification facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CB(7) the notification has the content the subsection requires` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the notification`'s `states that a disclosure request has been made`
           AND `the notification`'s `specifies the person to whom the request was made`
           AND ((NOT `the notification`'s `the request is made in connection with a suspicion of involvement in a terrorist financing offence`)
                OR (NOT `the notification`'s `the person suspected is known`)
                OR `the notification`'s `identifies the person suspected`)
           AND ((NOT `the notification`'s `the request is made in connection with the identification of terrorist property or of its movement or use`)
                OR (NOT `the notification`'s `the holder of the property is known`)
                OR `the notification`'s `identifies the property and the person who holds it`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the required notification must— (a) state that a disclosure request has been made; (b) specify the person to whom the request was made"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:242 | (8) A notification for the purposes of condition 5 in subsection (6) of section 21CA must—
-- src:243 | (a) state that a disclosure request is to be made;
-- src:244 | (b) specify the person to whom it is to be made;
-- src:245 | (c) describe the information to be sought in the request;
-- src:246 | (d) explain why the request is being made.
@ref s 21CB(8) (src:242-246)
GIVEN `the notification` IS A `Advance notification facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CB(8) the notification has the content the subsection requires` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the notification`'s `states that a disclosure request is to be made`
           AND `the notification`'s `specifies the person to whom it is to be made`
           AND `the notification`'s `describes the information to be sought in the request`
           AND `the notification`'s `explains why the request is being made`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notification for the purposes of condition 5 in subsection (6) of section 21CA must—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 21CC Effect on disclosures under section 21A`

-- src:248 | (1) This section applies if in any proceedings a question arises as to whether the required disclosure has been made—
-- src:249 | (a) by a person (A) who discloses information under section 21CA(1) as a result of a disclosure request,
-- src:250 | (b) by a person (B) who makes a required notification in accordance with section 21CB(5)(b), or
-- src:251 | (c) by any other person (C) to whom A discloses information under section 21CA(1) as a result of that request.
@ref s 21CC(1) (src:248-251)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Section 21CC applies facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CC(1) section 21CC applies` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `a question arises in proceedings as to whether the required disclosure has been made`
           AND (`the facts`'s `by a person who discloses information under s 21CA(1) as a result of a disclosure request`
                OR `the facts`'s `by a person who makes a required notification in accordance with s 21CB(5)(b)`
                OR `the facts`'s `by any other person to whom A discloses information under s 21CA(1) as a result of that request`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies if in any proceedings a question arises as to whether the required disclosure has been made"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:252 | (2) The making of a required notification in good faith is to be treated as satisfying any requirement to make the required disclosure on the part of A, B and C.
-- src:253 | This is subject to section 21CD(1) to (8).
@ref s 21CC(2) (src:252-253)
GIVEN `the required notification was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CC(2) the required notification satisfies the requirement to make the required disclosure` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the required notification was made` AND `it was made in good faith`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The making of a required notification in good faith is to be treated as satisfying any requirement" (a notification not made in good faith is not said to fail to satisfy it)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:254 | (3) The making of a joint disclosure report in good faith is to be treated as satisfying any requirement to make the required disclosure on the part of the persons who jointly make the report.
-- src:255 | This is subject to section 21CD(10).
@ref s 21CC(3) (src:254-255)
GIVEN `the joint disclosure report was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CC(3) the joint disclosure report satisfies the requirement to make the required disclosure` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the joint disclosure report was made` AND `it was made in good faith`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The making of a joint disclosure report in good faith is to be treated as satisfying any requirement" (a report not made in good faith is not said to fail to satisfy it)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:256 | (4) A joint disclosure report is a report to a constable that—
-- src:257 | (a) is made jointly by A and B (whether or not also jointly with other persons to whom A discloses information under section 21CA(1)),
-- src:258 | (b) satisfies the requirements as to content mentioned in subsection (5) or (as the case may be) subsection (6),
-- src:259 | (c) is prepared after the making of a disclosure by A to B under section 21CA(1) in connection with—
-- src:260 | (i) a suspicion of a person’s involvement in the commission of a terrorist financing offence, or
-- src:261 | (ii) the identification of terrorist property or of its movement or use, and
-- src:262 | (d) is sent to the constable before the end of the applicable period.
@ref s 21CC(4) (src:256-262)
GIVEN `made jointly by A and B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `content` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `prepared after A disclosed to B under s 21CA(1) in connection with a suspicion or the identification of terrorist property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sent before the end of the applicable period` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CC(4) the report is a joint disclosure report` IS
    `the conjunction` jointly `and also` rest
    WHERE
        jointly MEANS `the fact` `made jointly by A and B`
        prepared MEANS `the fact` `prepared after A disclosed to B under s 21CA(1) in connection with a suspicion or the identification of terrorist property`
        contentAndPrepared MEANS `the conjunction` content `and also` prepared
        rest MEANS `the conjunction` contentAndPrepared `and also` `sent before the end of the applicable period`

-- src:263 | (5) In the case of a joint disclosure report prepared in connection with a suspicion of a person’s involvement in the commission of a terrorist financing offence, the requirements as to content are that the report must—
-- src:264 | (a) explain the extent to which there are continuing grounds to suspect that the person is involved in the commission of the offence,
-- src:265 | (b) identify the person (if known),
-- src:266 | (c) set out the grounds for the suspicion, and
-- src:267 | (d) provide any other information relevant to the matter.
@ref s 21CC(5) (src:263-267)
GIVEN `the report` IS A `Suspicion report content facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CC(5) the report has the content required for a suspicion` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the report`'s `explains the extent to which there are continuing grounds to suspect that the person is involved in the commission of the offence`
           AND ((NOT `the report`'s `the person is known`) OR `the report`'s `identifies the person`)
           AND `the report`'s `sets out the grounds for the suspicion`
           AND `the report`'s `provides any other information relevant to the matter`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the requirements as to content are that the report must—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:268 | (6) In the case of a joint disclosure report prepared in connection with the identification of terrorist property or of its movement or use, the requirements as to content are that the report must—
-- src:269 | (a) explain the extent to which there are continuing grounds to suspect that the property is terrorist property,
-- src:270 | (b) identify the property and the person who holds it (if known),
-- src:271 | (c) provide details of its movement or use (if known), and
-- src:272 | (d) provide any other information relevant to the matter.
@ref s 21CC(6) (src:268-272)
GIVEN `the report` IS A `Property report content facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CC(6) the report has the content required for terrorist property` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the report`'s `explains the extent to which there are continuing grounds to suspect that the property is terrorist property`
           AND ((NOT `the report`'s `the property and the person who holds it are known`) OR `the report`'s `identifies the property and the person who holds it`)
           AND ((NOT `the report`'s `details of its movement or use are known`) OR `the report`'s `provides details of its movement or use`)
           AND `the report`'s `provides any other information relevant to the matter`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the requirements as to content are that the report must—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:276 | (8) A constable may vary the period of 28 days (whether by lengthening or shortening it) by giving written notice to the person who made the required notification.
@ref s 21CC(8) (src:276)
GIVEN `the notice is given by a constable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given to the person who made the required notification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CC(8) the notice varies the period of 28 days` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the notice is given by a constable` AND `the notice is in writing` AND `the notice is given to the person who made the required notification`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A constable may vary the period of 28 days (whether by lengthening or shortening it) by giving written notice to the person who made the required notification." (a notice by another person, or one that is not written, or one given to someone else, is outside the grant; the text does not say it fails to vary the period: fork F10, scope limit with no "only", ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 21CC(8) (src:276)
GIVEN `the length in days a constable set by written notice to the person who made the required notification` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 21CC(8) the length in days of the period of 28 days` IS
    CONSIDER `the length in days a constable set by written notice to the person who made the required notification`
    WHEN JUST days THEN days
    -- the base period, 28 days, stands when no variation was made by written notice (fork F10): "A constable may vary the period of 28 days (whether by lengthening or shortening it) by giving written notice"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 28

-- src:273 | (7) The applicable period is—
-- src:274 | (a) in a case where the disclosure under section 21CA was made as a result of a request from a constable by virtue of subsection (3)(a) of that section, whatever period may be specified by the constable when making the request;
-- src:275 | (b) in a case where the disclosure was made as a result of a request from another person by virtue of subsection (3)(b) of that section, the period of 28 days beginning with the day on which the notification is made for the purposes of condition 3 in section 21CA(4).
@ref s 21CC(7) (src:273-275)
GIVEN `who asked` IS A `Who asked for the disclosure`
      `the day the notification is made for the purposes of condition 3` IS A DATE
      `the length in days of the period of 28 days` IS A NUMBER
      `the last day the constable specified when making the request` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 21CC(7) the last day of the applicable period` IS
    CONSIDER `who asked`
    WHEN `a constable` THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "whatever period may be specified by the constable when making the request" (the constable's period is not in the Act; with none given, NOTHING)
        `the last day the constable specified when making the request`
    WHEN `a person mentioned in s 21CA(3)(b)` THEN
        -- the period "beginning with the day on which the notification is made" includes that day, so it ends 27 days later when it is 28 days long
        JUST (`the day the notification is made for the purposes of condition 3` + (`the length in days of the period of 28 days` - 1))

-- src:256 | (4) A joint disclosure report is a report to a constable that—
-- src:257 | (a) is made jointly by A and B (whether or not also jointly with other persons to whom A discloses information under section 21CA(1)),
-- src:258 | (b) satisfies the requirements as to content mentioned in subsection (5) or (as the case may be) subsection (6),
-- src:259 | (c) is prepared after the making of a disclosure by A to B under section 21CA(1) in connection with—
-- src:260 | (i) a suspicion of a person’s involvement in the commission of a terrorist financing offence, or
-- src:261 | (ii) the identification of terrorist property or of its movement or use, and
-- src:262 | (d) is sent to the constable before the end of the applicable period.
@ref s 21CC(4)(d) (src:256-262)
GIVEN `the day the report is sent to the constable` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the applicable period` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CC(4)(d) the report is sent to the constable before the end of the applicable period` IS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the applicable period`
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is sent to the constable before the end of the applicable period" (fork F9: the last day counts as inside the period)
        IF `the day the report is sent to the constable` AT MOST lastDay THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the period is the constable's, so with none given the text does not answer
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:277 | (9) A joint disclosure report must be—
-- src:278 | (a) approved by the nominated officer of each person that jointly makes the report, and
-- src:279 | (b) signed by the nominated officer on behalf of each such person.
-- src:280 | If there is no nominated officer the report must be approved and signed by another senior officer.
@ref s 21CC(9) (src:277-280)
GIVEN `the report` IS A `Report approval facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21CC(9) the joint disclosure report is approved and signed as required` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the report`'s `there is a nominated officer of each person that jointly makes the report`
            THEN (IF `the report`'s `approved by the nominated officer of each such person` AND `the report`'s `signed by the nominated officer on behalf of each such person` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If there is no nominated officer the report must be approved and signed by another senior officer."
        OTHERWISE (IF `the report`'s `approved and signed by another senior officer` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:281 | (10) References in this section to A, B or C include—
