    BRANCH
        IF `the information was obtained from a UK law enforcement agency` AND (NOT `that agency consents to the disclosure`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless that agency consents to the disclosure"
        IF `the information was obtained from a UK law enforcement agency`
            THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may not include information obtained from a UK law enforcement agency" (information from elsewhere is outside the bar)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:311 | (2) But a relevant disclosure may not include information obtained from a UK law enforcement agency unless that agency consents to the disclosure.
